{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1400810-rotes-and-rituals-and-instruments","id":1400810,"title":"Rotes and Rituals and Instruments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-03T12:23:11-07:00","id":1400810,"title":"Rotes and Rituals and Instruments","content":"Here are the HRs I have been using, now four sessions in, and so far it has worked out excellent. But it needs some more stress testing and maybe refinement. I am seeking criticism and advice for the rules as follow...<br /> * Normal run-of-the-mill improvises/fast-casting works as normal. Nothing is taken away, so you can ignore the HR and operate as normal with no disadvantage.<br /> * If the spell/weaving/effect is a Rote or cast as a Ritual of at least one interval (take some time even if it is just one roll), you may obtain an optional bonus of up to +1 die per additional Instrument <i>after</i> the first. Right now I have the limit st at Arete. I may want to reduce that.<br /> * If <b>both</b> a Rote and a Ritual, then there is an additional benefit in that 1's do not cancel Successes. A Botch still results if 1's outnumber successes, but otherwise you keep all Successes.<br /> * At least one Instrument is required unless Arete exceeds the highest Sphere by 2 points for a Mystic, or by 5 points if a Technomancer.<br /> * Technocrats must always use an Instrument<br /> * At least one Instrument is required for Ritual casting, no matter your Arete score.<br /> * Difficulty Modifiers still apply as normal. Multiple Modifiers may apply, specially in consideration of multiple Instruments, but each specific Modifier can only be used one. The max range is +/-3, but I want to maybe expand that to Avatar.<br /> <br /> The writing needs to be cleaned up, but that is the gist of it. I have it written out and printed elsewhere. Here, I wanted to rewrite it from memory as a stress test.<br /> I am also using the Rote points system from <i>Awakened Grimoire</i>, without the Sphere score bonus or the little extra modifiers. I told the players they can use any Rote from the books they have except for 1st edition. Some of those I may pass, but I want to see them first.<br /> <br /> There are three purposes that my HRs serve me. It is a matter if the balance against added complexity and hidden pitfalls is worth it.<br /> <br /> Purpose 1: I want higher casting dice pools. Not too crazy and not all the time. I want to be demanding of more successes, divided results option and all that.<br /> Purpose 2: I want to motivate players to use Rotes and have them written down. There is comfort and efficiency in knowing what you can do. I also think that they provide guide posts in navigating the field of potential improvisation.<br /> Purpose 3: I love the concept of Instruments, but the way a mage &quot;transcends&quot; the need feels a bit confusing and lacking in flavor. The Arete versus Rank idea came from another user here on this forum. I am bad at remembering names <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Sorry for that, but thanx for the idea<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T17:27:44-07:00","id":1400860,"title":"","content":"You might want to consider unawakened assistants an instrument for the purposes of how many you can stack. Otherwise Purpose 1 is going to be hard to balance with things like the Cult Background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T21:08:49-07:00","id":1400895,"title":"","content":"That is something I had not yet considered. And I do have one player with that Background. I will keep an eye on what they do. But for the most part, as long as they put the time in, I am comfortable with large dice pools.<br /> The *real* cap is the limit on the number of potential successes. I forget where that is found or what edition it is from. I *thing* (do not quote me) that the cap was Arete times Willpower. Or maybe that was an HR I read somewhere.<br /> I am placing a limit on Intervals. A number of rolls limited to Arete + Willpower. And, thanks to your insight, I am considering a cap on how large a casting dice pool can get. Arete + Willpower sounds reasonable.<br /> I am also using the divided successes option, so a mega feat such as drawing down the moon or Vampires-to-Lawnchairs will require 40 or more successes. Or maybe just 30? Or Fifty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T23:48:38-07:00","id":1400907,"title":"","content":"I thinking further and I think you are right. My solution adds a layer of complexity. I need to think in terms of a hard limit to how many bonus dice a Mage can gain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T18:24:37-07:00","id":1401030,"title":"","content":"Maybe it should be Half arete (rounded up)?<br /> &quot; If the spell/weaving/effect is a Rote or cast as a Ritual of at least one interval (take some time even if it is just one roll), you may obtain an optional bonus of up to +1 die per additional Instrument <i>after</i> the first. Right now I have the limit st at Arete. I may want to reduce that.&quot;<br /> So 1-2 Arete = 1 Bonus dice, 3-4 2, etc. Otherwise you get a ton of extra dice which, from what I've read in M20 so far, are rather rare and hard to come by (Compared to a simple DC minus). Also it supports: Use more instruments. Without saying: Use every fucking instrument you know just cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}